---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Features — SIKKA";
const description = "SIKKA features — Zero fees, no transaction history, ML-DSA-87 post-quantum cryptography, native multisig, credit-based spam control.";
const path = "/features.html";
const jsonLd = undefined;

---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} jsonLd={jsonLd} active="features">

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="label">Protocol Features</span>
    <h1>Everything <span class="gradient-text">Different</span></h1>
    <p>SIKKA rethinks every layer of a digital currency — from the ledger structure to the cryptography to the network transport.</p>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="bento">

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-6 reveal">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;">
          <div class="bento-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i></div>
          <span class="tag green"><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i> Always</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bento-title">Zero Fees — Forever</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">When you send SIKKA, the exact amount arrives in full. There are no gas fees, no priority fees, no miner tips, no protocol cuts. Zero. The recipient receives exactly what you sent — always.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
          <div style="font-size:2.5rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-0.05em;" class="gradient-text">$0.00</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-3);">Per transaction, any amount, forever</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-6 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="bento-icon purple"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-secret"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">No Transaction History</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">SIKKA keeps balances, not a public ledger of every payment. Transactions are batched into checkpoints, consensus signs the state root, and the transactions are then discarded. Past payments are not reconstructable — private by default.</div>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:0.5rem;">
          <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem;text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--purple-2);">0</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-3);">Public tx logs</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem;text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--blue-2);">SMT</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-3);">State proof</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal">
        <div class="bento-icon cyan"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">Checkpoint Consensus</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">Round-robin proposers batch transactions into a checkpoint. Validators vote and a checkpoint finalizes once ≥2/3 of the bonded stake agrees.</div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="bento-icon green"><i class="fa-solid fa-scale-balanced"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">Atomic Account Balances</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">Transfers debit the sender and credit the recipient atomically in CHILLAR integer arithmetic. No gas, no change outputs, no rounding — the recipient gets exactly what you send.</div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="bento-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-database"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">Account-Based, Pure-Rust</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">Balances live in a tiny ACID key-value store on top of <code style="font-family:monospace;color:var(--cyan);">redb</code>. Three fixed tables, zero C/C++ dependencies. Storage grows with accounts, not with every transfer.</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section" style="background:var(--bg-1);border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
      <span class="label">Spam Resistance</span>
      <h2>Per-Account <span class="gradient-text">Spend Credits</span></h2>
      <p>No useless proof-of-work. Instead every account earns spend credits that regenerate over time — enough for daily use, too slow for abuse.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;align-items:start;" class="reveal">
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;">
          <table class="pow-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Account State</th>
                <th>Credit Rate</th>
                <th>Cap</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Active wallet</td>
                <td class="mono">+1 / minute</td>
                <td class="mono">100</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Fresh account</td>
                <td class="mono">starts at 0</td>
                <td class="mono">—</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Each transaction</td>
                <td class="mono">burns 1</td>
                <td class="mono">—</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-3);margin-top:0.75rem;">Starting at 0 credits prevents funding-sybil attacks. Credits regenerate over time, so normal use is free and sustained spam is impossible.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1.5rem;">
          <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;margin-bottom:1rem;">Credit balance over time (capped at 100)</div>
          <div class="chart-wrap lg">
            <canvas id="chart-congestion"></canvas>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
      <span class="label">Security</span>
      <h2>Post-Quantum by <span class="gradient-text">Design</span></h2>
      <p>No classical elliptic curve fallbacks. Every key, every signature, every hash uses algorithms hardened against quantum computers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento">

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-8 reveal" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(59,130,246,0.08),rgba(139,92,246,0.06));border-color:rgba(59,130,246,0.25);">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <div>
            <div class="bento-icon purple" style="width:52px;height:52px;font-size:1.3rem;"><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i></div>
          </div>
          <div style="flex:1;min-width:200px;">
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
              <div class="bento-title" style="font-size:1.3rem;">ML-DSA-87</div>
              <span class="tag purple">NIST FIPS 204</span>
              <span class="tag green">Post-Quantum</span>
            </div>
            <div class="bento-desc">SIKKA uses Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Algorithm at the highest security level (87 = NIST Level 5). This is the strongest post-quantum signature standard published by NIST. There are no classical ECDSA or Ed25519 fallbacks — every signature in SIKKA is quantum-resistant by default.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1rem;">
          <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--blue-2);">Level 5</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-3);">NIST Security</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--purple-2);">4,595B</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-3);">Signature size</div>
          </div>
          <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem;text-align:center;">
            <div style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--green);">0</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-3);">Classical fallbacks</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="bento-icon yellow"><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">Cryptography Stack</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:160px;">
          <canvas id="chart-crypto"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;font-size:0.78rem;color:var(--text-2);">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;"><span style="width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--blue);flex-shrink:0;"></span>ML-DSA-87 — Signatures</div>
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;"><span style="width:10px;height:10px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--yellow);flex-shrink:0;"></span>SHA3-256 — Hashing &amp; SMT</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <div class="bento-icon purple"><i class="fa-solid fa-users"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">Native Multisig</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">Up to 16 co-signers can collaboratively build and sign a single transaction. True m-of-n multisig at the protocol layer — no smart contracts, no bytecode, no extra attack surface.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:auto;">
          <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:900;color:var(--purple-2);">16-of-16</div>
          <div style="font-size:0.78rem;color:var(--text-3);">Maximum co-signers</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      
      <div class="bento-card bento-4 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <div class="bento-icon green"><i class="fa-solid fa-globe"></i></div>
        <div class="bento-title">HTTP Federation</div>
        <div class="bento-desc">Nodes federate over a clean HTTP API. Light clients, wallets, and explorers can query any node. The same API powers the built-in web wallet and explorer.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:auto;"><span class="tag blue">REST API</span></div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="cta-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:1rem;">Go Deeper</span>
      <h2>See how it all <span class="gradient-text">fits together</span></h2>
      <p>Explore the architecture — checkpoint consensus, transaction lifecycle, finality, and tokenomics.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="index.html#architecture" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg"><i class="fa-solid fa-sitemap"></i> View Architecture</a>
        <a href="run-node.html" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg"><i class="fa-solid fa-server"></i> Run a Node</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script is:inline src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/chart.js/4.4.0/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
  </Fragment>
  <script>import '../scripts/charts.js';</script>
  <script>import '../scripts/main.js';</script>
</BaseLayout>
